                        ],
                        "form": "constellated"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "efd046ea-2051-33da-a680-433a392f90d3",
                        "entry_id": "029b7683-4d1b-3807-a024-65eddcac5332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To combine as a cluster."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "392f2bc0-e54f-4864-a052-0505aa9a7913",
                                "sense_id": "efd046ea-2051-33da-a680-433a392f90d3",
                                "text": "[…] he who is solicitous for his own improvement, must not suffer his endeavours to be limited by local reputation, but select from every tribe of mortals their characteristical virtues, and constellate in himself the scattered graces which shine single in other men."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "baf36b19-e75d-355a-b147-4a085388efc9",
                        "entry_id": "029b7683-4d1b-3807-a024-65eddcac5332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To fit, adorn (as if) with constellations."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9a094a9d-8bfa-48a2-a6e3-ce0f2bf66528",
                                "sense_id": "baf36b19-e75d-355a-b147-4a085388efc9",
                                "text": "What Artist now dares boast that he can bring\nHeaven hither, or constellate any thing,\nSo as the influence of those starres may bee\nImprisond in an Herbe, or Charme, or Tree,\nAnd doe by touch, all which those starres could do?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f350972c-d8aa-4a00-8fca-0003d4e939c8",
                                "sense_id": "baf36b19-e75d-355a-b147-4a085388efc9",
                                "text": "The abbot was not merely accused of rape and murder; the crime of sorcery was laid to his charge, as well as to Matilda’s. […] To criminate the monk, the constellated mirror was produced, which Matilda had accidentally left in his chamber."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7978870b-9964-4327-b492-bf289d9532cb",
                                "sense_id": "baf36b19-e75d-355a-b147-4a085388efc9",
                                "text": "There grew pied wind-flowers and violets,\nDaisies, those pearled Arcturi of the earth,\nThe constellated flower that never sets;"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6ce80284-b3ec-4cf8-b52d-7dec89bcdeb6",
                                "sense_id": "baf36b19-e75d-355a-b147-4a085388efc9",
                                "text": "[…] even the constellated glories of Paradise Lost are less moving than the plain words wherein Samson [Agonistes] forecasts his approaching end […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3ef72ba5-86b1-3a22-a78e-f24b1f7ccdf1",
                        "entry_id": "029b7683-4d1b-3807-a024-65eddcac5332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To (form a) cluster."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "689077c0-169b-461d-aa1a-7b5ed4e99611",
                                "sense_id": "3ef72ba5-86b1-3a22-a78e-f24b1f7ccdf1",
                                "text": "It’s no surprise that so much fiction constellates around the subject of Henry and his wives."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbad1776-18bf-31f1-8f57-c059564f0141",
                        "entry_id": "029b7683-4d1b-3807-a024-65eddcac5332",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To shine with united radiance, or one general light."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "intransitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b8d3a734-f781-4e9d-bfb9-67fd42292385",
                                "sense_id": "bbad1776-18bf-31f1-8f57-c059564f0141",
                                "text": "[…] the several things which are wont most to Engage and Heighten our affections, do, in a peculiar and transcendent manner, Shine forth and Constellate in God."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0ef0ce56-68d5-4fe5-b672-4d927b5bcf37",
                        "source_entry_id": "029b7683-4d1b-3807-a024-65eddcac5332",
                        "source_sense_description": "fit, adorn with constellations",
                        "target_lang_word": "consteller",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "consteller",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1dc7c9cb-9453-3bf1-a867-66160163620b",
                                        "entry_id": "a91adb51-f52c-3390-91f1-62ba97b1089e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parsemer d'étoiles, de choses brillantes comme des étoiles."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4da3f16e-32f7-4e5e-8ff8-9511ebda9656",
                                                "sense_id": "1dc7c9cb-9453-3bf1-a867-66160163620b",
                                                "text": "Des perles, des paillettes constellaient sa robe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "80f158bb-c352-4138-b658-70e44100396a",
                                                "sense_id": "1dc7c9cb-9453-3bf1-a867-66160163620b",
                                                "text": "Au total, 5 000 satellites constellent donc le ciel actuellement."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "faa82800-1efe-3a20-83ba-be93b400ddb1",
                                        "entry_id": "a91adb51-f52c-3390-91f1-62ba97b1089e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Parsemer."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "12ec5a79-c9c1-41dc-9349-8111f102eee6",
                                                "sense_id": "faa82800-1efe-3a20-83ba-be93b400ddb1",
                                                "text": "Mais cela peut même aller jusqu’à la désertification lorsque les familles ont pu à leur tour migrer : la montagne kabyle ou libanaise est ainsi constellée de fermes abandonnées."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e32f8d46-7af7-4778-8c0e-f4d71e0da2ca",
                                                "sense_id": "faa82800-1efe-3a20-83ba-be93b400ddb1",
                                                "text": "J’éprouvai une vague envie d’écraser entre mes longues griffes d’agate les points noirs qui constellaient les ailes de son nez en sueur."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
